<title> Peripheral Neuropathy, Distal-Symmetric: Diagnosis.</title>
<graphic href="eee0452-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Suspected distal-symmetric polyneuropathy: Patient complaining of numbness, burning, or prickling, confined to or predominantly located in the feet</label>
<path target="cell-2"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Clincial examination: decreased or absent ankle reflexes and decreased distal sensation?</label>
<path target="cell-3">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-4">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Medical history of diabetes mellitus?</label>
<path target="cell-6">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-5">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-5">
<label>Laboratory screening informative?*</label>
<path target="cell-6">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-7">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-7">
<label>Neurophysiological examination</label>
<path target="cell-9">Demyelinating</path>
<path target="cell-8">Axonal or normal</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-8">
<label>Patient more than 60 years of age, predominantly sensory symptoms?</label>
<path target="cell-10">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-9">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-10">
<label>Rapid progression of symptoms?</label>
<path target="cell-9">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-11">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-11">
<label>Family history informative?</label>
<path target="cell-13">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-12">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-12">
<label>Chronic idiopathic axonal polyneuropathy (CIAP) is likely.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-13">
<label>Hereditary neuropathy.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-4">
<label>Consider other diagnoses.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>Clue to etiology (e.g., diabetic, toxic, uremic, vitamin deficient, ...): initiate specific therapy.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-9">
<label>Refer for further neurological evaluation.</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>*CBC, electrolytes, BUN, hepatic transaminases, vitamin B1 and B12, paraprotein screen, TSH, ESR, and serum ACE.</footnote>
</footnotes>
</algorithm>
